{#
	The plain-text half of an invitation (XIV-1).

	Written by hand rather than derived from the HTML one, for the reason
	RenderedEmail gives: a text part made by stripping tags out of a table layout
	is a text part nobody would want to read. It is short enough that keeping the
	two in step is not a burden.

	The URL is on its own line and nothing else is, because that is what makes a
	mail client turn it into something clickable — and this message has exactly
	one job.
#}
